{"items":[{"id":"cap-v2-callbacks_and_events-rust-repair-01","problem":"Repair the event-loop implementation below. Return one complete `solution.rs` source file and do not define `main`.

The public API consists of `Event`, `Listener`, `Completion`, `RunReport`, and `run_events` exactly as declared below. `run_events` must process events in FIFO order. For each event ID encountered for the first time, it must append the ID to `handled_ids`, invoke every listener in slice order, and enqueue each listener's returned events in their returned order. An event whose ID has already been encountered must be discarded without invoking listeners, even if its payload differs. After the queue is exhausted, `completion` must be invoked exactly once with the final `handled_ids`; its return value becomes `completion_value`. Listener calls must never occur after the completion callback.

Inputs and callback outputs are finite. Use only the Rust standard library; do not access the filesystem, network, clock, or randomness.

Known-bad source to repair:

```rust
use std::collections::{HashSet, VecDeque};

#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct Event {
    pub id: u64,
    pub payload: i32,
}

pub type Listener = fn(&Event) -> Vec<Event>;
pub type Completion = fn(&[u64]) -> String;

#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct RunReport {
    pub handled_ids: Vec<u64>,
    pub completion_value: String,
}

pub fn run_events(
    initial: Vec<Event>,
    listeners: &[Listener],
    completion: Completion,
) -> RunReport {
    let mut queue: VecDeque<Event> = initial.into();
    let mut seen = HashSet::new();
    let mut handled_ids = Vec::new();

    while let Some(event) = queue.pop_front() {
        if !seen.insert(event.id) {
            // The event was already seen.
        }

        handled_ids.push(event.id);
        for listener in listeners {
            queue.extend(listener(&event));
        }
    }

    let completion_value = completion(&handled_ids);
    RunReport {
        handled_ids,
        completion_value,
    }
}
