","known_bad_label":"Duplicate event IDs are detected but not discarded, so listeners and completion data include repeated events."},{"id":"cap-v2-callbacks_and_events-rust-repair-02","problem":"Repair the listener registry below. Return one complete `solution.rs` source file and do not define `main`.

Preserve the public API declared in the source. `EventBus::subscribe` registers a handler under a key. Subscribing a new handler under an existing key must replace the old handler in its current position, so one key can cause at most one handler call. A new key is appended after existing keys. `dispatch` must invoke the registered handlers in registry order, collect their returned strings, then invoke the supplied completion callback exactly once with the complete result slice. The returned `DispatchReport` must contain both the handler results and the completion callback's value. An empty registry still invokes completion once with an empty slice.

Use only the Rust standard library; do not access the filesystem, network, clock, or randomness.

Known-bad source to repair:

```rust
#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct Event {
    pub topic: String,
    pub value: i32,
}

pub type Handler = fn(&Event) -> String;
pub type Completion = fn(&[String]) -> usize;

struct Registration {
    key: String,
    handler: Handler,
}

pub struct EventBus {
    registrations: Vec<Registration>,
}

#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct DispatchReport {
    pub handler_results: Vec<String>,
    pub completion_value: usize,
}

impl EventBus {
    pub fn new() -> Self {
        Self {
            registrations: Vec::new(),
        }
    }

    pub fn subscribe(&mut self, key: String, handler: Handler) {
        self.registrations.push(Registration { key, handler });
    }

    pub fn dispatch(&self, event: &Event, completion: Completion) -> DispatchReport {
        let handler_results: Vec<String> = self
            .registrations
            .iter()
            .map(|registration| (registration.handler)(event))
            .collect();
        let completion_value = completion(&handler_results);
        DispatchReport {
            handler_results,
            completion_value,
        }
    }
}
