","known_bad_label":"Nodes are emitted before their dependencies, producing preorder instead of the required depth-first postorder."},{"id":"cap-v2-graph_and_tree-rust-generation-02","problem":"Implement shared-node path traversal in one complete `solution.rs` source file. Do not define `main`.

Expose exactly this public API:

```rust
#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct SceneNode {
    pub name: String,
    pub children: Vec<usize>,
}

#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct SceneGraph {
    pub nodes: Vec<SceneNode>,
}

pub fn leaf_paths(graph: &SceneGraph, root: usize) -> Vec<Vec<usize>>;
```

Node IDs are indices in `graph.nodes`. Inputs are guaranteed to use valid indices and form a directed acyclic graph. Return every root-to-leaf path, with each path containing both its root and leaf IDs. A leaf is a node with no children. Traverse children left to right, which also determines result order.

The graph may use aliasing: the same child node may be referenced by several parents. Such a shared node must be traversed separately through every incoming path; do not globally suppress repeated node IDs. For example, if root `0` has children `1` and `2`, and both have child `3`, return `[[0, 1, 3], [0, 2, 3]]`.

Borrow the graph immutably and keep the current path in separate traversal state. Do not clone or mutate graph nodes. Use only the Rust standard library and do not access the filesystem, network, clock, or randomness.","reference_code":"#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct SceneNode {
    pub name: String,
    pub children: Vec<usize>,
}

#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct SceneGraph {
    pub nodes: Vec<SceneNode>,
}

pub fn leaf_paths(graph: &SceneGraph, root: usize) -> Vec<Vec<usize>> {
    fn walk(
        graph: &SceneGraph,
        node: usize,
        current: &mut Vec<usize>,
        output: &mut Vec<Vec<usize>>,
    ) {
        current.push(node);

        if graph.nodes[node].children.is_empty() {
            output.push(current.clone());
        } else {
            for &child in &graph.nodes[node].children {
                walk(graph, child, current, output);
            }
        }

        current.pop();
    }

    let mut output = Vec::new();
    let mut current = Vec::new();
    walk(graph, root, &mut current, &mut output);
    output
}
","known_bad_code":"#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct SceneNode {
